entire trail show — Show trail intent and its repositories and branches
Show a project trail by its project-local number or ULID, or the trail of <repo>/<number> branch work. Without a selector, follow the current branch's parent. Use --branch to follow another branch's parent. Open changes, and the change the trail was reached through, show their merge gates (the first 20 changes).

When to use this:
Trail commands talk to entire.io and read the saved login from the OS
keyring (the Keychain on macOS), so they need network and keyring access.
If you run commands in a sandbox, request unsandboxed execution for
`entire trail` up front. An error saying the Keychain is not accessible or
the network is not allowed means the sandbox blocked it, not that the user
is logged out: ask to re-run it unsandboxed, and do not run `entire login`.

A project trail spans repositories; each change is its branch in one
repository. Project trails and changes are numbered separately: never
pass <P> where a change is expected, or <n> where a project trail is.
Pass <repo>/<n> to checkout, resume, finding, watch, approvals or
approve; given to show, it shows the parent project trail.
Users paste Entire trail URLs. Do not pass a URL to any command; map
the path after the host to a selector:
  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<repo>/<n>  change <repo>/<n>
  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<n>  change <repo>/<n>
  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/trails/<n>                change <repo>/<n>
  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>                     project trail <P>
Add --project <forge>/<project> unless <project> is origin's owner.
To link a trail or change, use the url `entire trail show` prints.

To list a project trail's changes, run `entire trail show <P>
--project <forge>/<project> --json`; each changes[] entry is the change
<repository>/<number> with its own url and base (the branch it merges
into). When show reaches the trail through a change (the current
branch, --branch, or <repo>/<n>), that entry has current: true; link
its url, the change's page, in preference to the top-level url, the
whole trail's page. When asked to act on
(e.g. review) a whole project trail, cover every change. Checkout and
review need a clone of that repository: do the ones in this clone and
tell the user which changes need another clone instead of skipping
them silently. A change's merge state is changes[].mergeability: its
gates (approvals, checks, findings, up_to_date) are under .gates and
its CI runs, with details_url links, under .checks.runs. mergeability
is null for merged or closed changes other than the current one, when
the server has no snapshot yet, and when it could not be read; only a
failed read prints a warning on stderr. Null is unknown, never
mergeable.

Current repo: gh/llLucidll/VEGA  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)

Flags:
      --branch string       Discover the project trail through this repository branch (defaults to current branch when no trail is given)
      --json[=true|false]   Output raw JSON instead of a table

Inherited flags:
      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)
      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace
      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project

